0.7903C9.21755 10.7903 9.42552 10.7515 9.6181 10.6805L11.1528 12.7929C10.5174 13.1549 9.78278 13.362 9.00065 13.362C8.21852 13.362 7.48392 13.1549 6.84847 12.7929ZM11.9422 12.2179L10.4074 10.1054C10.6473 9.80079 10.791 9.41697 10.791 8.99998C10.791 8.97726 10.7901 8.95473 10.7893 8.93221L13.2744 8.12475C13.3322 8.4076 13.3626 8.70031 13.3626 8.99998C13.3626 10.2727 12.8146 11.4198 11.9422 12.2179Z21:T578,you couldn't even get my oil change right. I told ya my car needed 0W20. I told you in the beginning you didn't even listen. thank god I saw your guy grab the wrong oil (5W40) other wise I would have driven home without knowing my car got a wrong oil change . I also came for amsoil and you got me something completely different. The wrong oil you put in my car was not amsoil and the later one you changed was not amsoil either after you realized you made a mistake. The oil was something from a steel drum. who knows what's inside there and the guy who pump the oil out the drum didn't even know how much he should pump. at that point I already felt unsafe and I quickly googled another service center that had amsoil and was just a few miles away. I went there (my car was already driving weird tho) and the manager or supervisor immediately knew what oil my car needed and how much it needed after lookup in his computer. He brought the oil to me and it's exactly the amsoil my car uses. I changed the oil again there and what upset me again was that the tech told me the oil filter was leaking. What a nice job you have done. and after failing to perform this basic work, you still charged me 150$, for unknown quality of oil and unfit oil filter. do you even feel shame? stop throwing those BS canned messages like \"Please call us at 516-518-5552\" to show you care but in fact you don't at all.23:T578,you couldn't even get my oil change right. I told ya my car needed 0W20. I told you in the beginning you didn't even listen. thank god I saw your guy grab the wrong oil (5W40) other wise "])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"I would have driven home without knowing my car got a wrong oil change . I also came for amsoil and you got me something completely different. The wrong oil you put in my car was not amsoil and the later one you changed was not amsoil either after you realized you made a mistake. The oil was something from a steel drum. who knows what's inside there and the guy who pump the oil out the drum didn't even know how much he should pump. at that point I already felt unsafe and I quickly googled another service center that had amsoil and was just a few miles away. I went there (my car was already driving weird tho) and the manager or supervisor immediately knew what oil my car needed and how much it needed after lookup in his computer. He brought the oil to me and it's exactly the amsoil my car uses. I changed the oil again there and what upset me again was that the tech told me the oil filter was leaking. What a nice job you have done. and after failing to perform this basic work, you still charged me 150$, for unknown quality of oil and unfit oil filter. do you even feel shame? stop throwing those BS canned messages like \"Please call us at 516-518-5552\" to show you care but in fact you don't at all."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"13:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$1b\"}}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"flex justify-center py-6 md:py-9 lg:py-12 bg-white\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative w-full px-[16px] sm:px-[24px] md:px-0 md:max-w-md lg:max-w-lg xl:max-w-xl 2xl:max-w-2xl\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"font-bold text-2xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl xl:text-5xl 2xl:text-7xl text-neutral-900 md:absolute top-8 lg:top-14 xl:top-8 2xl:top-12 flex md:flex-col\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Let's Find Your \"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"classNa